    - new_regen_workflow.py runs on the standard library (PyYAML only adds the parse check, with a note when absent); --mode local writes
      regenerate.yml when it is missing (a caller without its callee fails on GitHub at parse time); both caller modes pass exactly
      REGEN_TOKEN; --on schedule without a cron is a usage error; a note names the branch the triggers were written for when the clone's
      origin/HEAD differs; --help names REGEN_TOKEN
    - update_readme_index.py lists the files of a directory first, then its sub-directories, case-insensitive
    - SKILL.md: prerequisites, "In another repository" (copy the folder, inline is self-contained, local is one command, remote needs the
      host's file, private callers only), protected-branch remedy, concurrency and loop-guard wording, examples aligned with the committed
      caller; github-actions-facts.md updated
    - diff_ledger.py: the INDEX.md header names the Regenerated-by skip and is refreshed when the header text changes; aider-scaffold
      SKILL.md notes both skips
    - ci.yml and the README verify block check the README index; tests: 15 (optional PyYAML, schedule error, local emits its callee,
      index order, one secret in both callers)
    
